WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.507
"32nd Aozora Festival"

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:16.935
H-Have you decided?

00:00:18.228 --> 00:00:21.189
"Helper"

00:00:21.272 --> 00:00:23.149
Don't act so depressed.

00:00:23.358 --> 00:00:24.817
I'm not depressed.

00:00:25.026 --> 00:00:26.653
You're so easy to read.

00:00:26.861 --> 00:00:27.403
Ow!

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:29.781
You're taking it out on me?

00:00:31.282 --> 00:00:32.909
Mashiki's not here, huh?

00:00:33.117 --> 00:00:34.494
Yeah.

00:00:34.702 --> 00:00:37.413
That's unfortunate for you.
It's the day of the festival.

00:00:37.622 --> 00:00:38.873
Does she have a cold or something?

00:00:39.082 --> 00:00:41.042
A cold?

00:00:43.962 --> 00:00:47.465
Mashiki, are you...

00:00:47.674 --> 00:00:50.552
Uh, Mashiki?

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:53.388
--Is something--
--I'm sorry.

00:00:53.596 --> 00:00:54.597
What?

00:01:00.937 --> 00:01:02.647
| might've done it this time.

00:01:02.855 --> 00:01:03.773
You...!

00:01:03.982 --> 00:01:06.234
You mean to Mashiki?

00:01:06.442 --> 00:01:07.277
Huh?

00:01:07.485 --> 00:01:09.153
You didn't tell me about that.

00:01:09.362 --> 00:01:11.823
As another dude, I understand how you feel,

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:13.825
but you're not supposed to
do that without consent.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.868
What?

00:01:17.912 --> 00:01:21.583
No, you idiot! What were you thinking of?

00:01:21.791 --> 00:01:23.084
So, what did you do?

00:01:23.293 --> 00:01:26.546
| think she's avoiding me.

00:01:26.754 --> 00:01:28.089
Because you confessed your feelings to her?

00:01:28.298 --> 00:01:31.426
I... didn't tell her.

00:01:33.803 --> 00:01:34.387
Ow!

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:36.848
That's enough.

00:01:37.056 --> 00:01:38.850
You guys seem rather close.

00:01:39.058 --> 00:01:40.560
Sorry.

00:01:42.103 --> 00:01:43.855
There's nothing wrong with lively.

00:01:44.063 --> 00:01:46.482
You've been helping us out a lot.

00:01:46.691 --> 00:01:47.483
We appreciate it.

00:01:47.692 --> 00:01:50.153
Nice, Senpai. I knew you'd understand.

00:01:50.361 --> 00:01:52.405
Hey, don't let it go to your head.

00:01:52.614 --> 00:01:53.823
Whoops.

00:01:55.116 --> 00:01:56.701
"Where are you? It's almost
time for your shift."

00:01:56.701 --> 00:01:56.993
"Where are you? It's almost
time for your shift." Is it your shift?

00:01:56.993 --> 00:01:57.827
Is it your shift?

00:01:58.036 --> 00:02:00.747
Yeah. I'll have someone else cover for me.

00:02:00.955 --> 00:02:05.960
It's fine. It's nearly
time for my shift, too.

00:02:06.169 --> 00:02:08.171
Excuse us.

00:02:16.804 --> 00:02:20.600
I'm jealous of everything those
first-years have going on.

00:02:20.808 --> 00:02:23.186
It's almost heartwarming.

00:02:23.394 --> 00:02:25.396
| don't think so.

00:02:25.605 --> 00:02:26.981
What?

00:02:28.107 --> 00:02:34.739
Sometimes people's feelings
never amount to anything.

00:02:42.622 --> 00:02:44.749
Brother.

00:02:45.708 --> 00:02:46.918
Hurry.

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:48.002
You'll trip.

00:02:48.211 --> 00:02:49.629
What?

00:02:51.839 --> 00:02:52.882
What did I just say?

00:02:53.091 --> 00:02:54.384
Sorry.

00:02:54.592 --> 00:02:57.762
Once you're in high school,
you'll have to pull yourself together.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.097
Okay.

00:02:59.097 --> 00:03:00.515
"New Student Information"
"Aokisora High School" Okay.

00:03:00.515 --> 00:03:00.723
"New Student Information"
"Aokisora High School"

00:03:00.723 --> 00:03:03.101
<i>"New Student Information” " Aokisora High School" We'll
be attending the same school starting this spring.</i>

00:03:03.309 --> 00:03:05.061
Yeah.

00:03:11.025 --> 00:03:11.776
What is it?

00:03:11.984 --> 00:03:13.569
It's frozen.

00:03:13.778 --> 00:03:15.405
Can we cross it?

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:16.656
It's dangerous.

00:03:16.864 --> 00:03:19.826
Apparently there's a
story behind this bridge.

00:03:20.034 --> 00:03:21.619
What?

00:03:23.037 --> 00:03:24.288
Sheesh.

00:03:24.497 --> 00:03:26.791
There's a weird rumor surrounding it.

00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:31.337
At my school, they call
it "The Lovers' Bridge."

00:03:31.546 --> 00:03:34.006
"The Lovers' Bridge"?

00:03:34.215 --> 00:03:36.592
That's nice.

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:38.720
You think so?

00:03:55.695 --> 00:03:56.404
I gotta stand up now

00:03:56.404 --> 00:03:58.364
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"
I gotta stand up now

00:03:58.364 --> 00:03:59.198
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"

00:03:59.198 --> 00:04:00.324
"Convenience Store Boy Friends"
A devil with the face of an angel--feel so bad

00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:05.621
A devil with the face of an angel--feel so bad

00:04:05.830 --> 00:04:11.461
I lift my face; sighs don't suit me

00:04:11.669 --> 00:04:12.712
Damn it

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:16.799
Someone's voice asks, "How's everyone doing?"

00:04:17.008 --> 00:04:19.510
How we do right now, hey hey hey

00:04:19.719 --> 00:04:24.474
I can't stand up yet--right:
get moving by confronting it head-on

00:04:24.682 --> 00:04:25.850
The deciding touchdown!

00:04:26.058 --> 00:04:29.061
One, two, come on!
Kick it to the curb

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.774
Third-day troubles--no sweat!
We're gonna make you say

00:04:32.982 --> 00:04:35.151
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:04:35.359 --> 00:04:36.110
Let me hear you say

00:04:36.319 --> 00:04:38.070
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:04:38.279 --> 00:04:40.031
I gotta stand up now

00:04:40.239 --> 00:04:43.451
Oh, more laughs tonight

00:04:43.659 --> 00:04:46.746
Life is the best--c'mon, face up now

00:04:46.954 --> 00:04:51.709
Oh, more laughs tonight--take life face up

00:04:51.918 --> 00:04:54.837
I gotta stand up now

00:04:55.046 --> 00:04:57.924
One, two, come on! Kick it to the curb

00:04:58.132 --> 00:05:01.677
Third-day troubles--no sweat!
We're gonna make you say

00:05:01.886 --> 00:05:04.472
Yeah, yeah, yeah

00:05:05.765 --> 00:05:08.935
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:05:09.143 --> 00:05:12.438
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:05:12.647 --> 00:05:15.775
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:05:15.983 --> 00:05:19.779
Oh, I gotta stand up now

00:05:20.363 --> 00:05:24.826
"October"

00:05:27.745 --> 00:05:30.373
"Student Council Elections"
"Grab the future with your hand!!"

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.543
Student council elections, huh?

00:05:33.751 --> 00:05:36.838
Well, not that it concerns me.

00:05:37.046 --> 00:05:41.217
Watching Nakajima-senpai makes being on
the student council seem like a lot of work.

00:05:41.425 --> 00:05:43.719
| wouldn't do it even if they asked me to.

00:05:43.928 --> 00:05:49.684
Actually, I can never say "no" to people.

00:05:49.892 --> 00:05:53.646
Hey! Are you listening to...

00:06:16.043 --> 00:06:19.922
"Student Council Election"

00:06:21.757 --> 00:06:22.884
Did everyone get one?

00:06:23.092 --> 00:06:25.469
Who didn't get one?

00:06:29.599 --> 00:06:33.978
Uh, does anyone have any questions?

00:06:35.646 --> 00:06:38.649
"Current student council members will complete their terms on
12/15. Incoming members should be trained between 12/8 - 12/15."

00:06:51.996 --> 00:06:53.331
Come in.

00:06:53.539 --> 00:06:55.541
Excuse the intrusion.

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:58.210
Ugh, it's a mess.

00:06:58.419 --> 00:07:02.256
This always happens when you're busy.

00:07:02.465 --> 00:07:04.634
Are you listening?

00:07:04.842 --> 00:07:06.177
You can leave them there.

00:07:06.385 --> 00:07:09.138
| won't be able to find them later.

00:07:09.347 --> 00:07:12.099
Can you find anything now?

00:07:12.308 --> 00:07:13.392
You're so weird.

00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:15.811
Sorry I'm weird. Don't touch anything.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:21.108
Okay. Sakurakoji-senpai is amazing.

00:07:21.317 --> 00:07:24.236
| can't believe he can
handle being around you.

00:07:24.445 --> 00:07:27.031
Yeah, I can't manage without him.

00:07:27.239 --> 00:07:28.532
Seriously.

00:07:28.741 --> 00:07:33.371
You should be thanking
me and Sakurakoji-senpai.

00:07:33.579 --> 00:07:34.747
Not you, Waka.

00:07:34.956 --> 00:07:36.999
You're so mean.

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:46.801
Are you busy preparing for the election?

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:48.552
More or less.

00:07:48.761 --> 00:07:52.014
Preparing for my successor takes up more
of my time than the actual election.

00:07:52.223 --> 00:07:55.685
| need to make sure the next president
doesn't have any problems.

00:07:55.893 --> 00:07:59.021
You're a perfect president, aren't you?

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:01.399
You really are amazing.

00:08:01.607 --> 00:08:04.735
I'm so proud of you, Brother.

00:08:04.944 --> 00:08:07.196
"Brother," huh?

00:08:07.405 --> 00:08:09.281
Hey.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:13.869
Hello. Thanks for all your help.

00:08:14.078 --> 00:08:16.622
It's fine.

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.418
Are you here to see Mikado? Should I leave?

00:08:20.626 --> 00:08:25.840
No, I just thought we could go home
together if he was finishing soon.

00:08:26.048 --> 00:08:28.009
Sorry. I won't be finished
for a while longer.

00:08:28.217 --> 00:08:31.554
| see. Well, I did want
to ask you something.

00:08:31.762 --> 00:08:34.598
Okay. I'll call you when I get home.

00:08:34.807 --> 00:08:38.394
Okay. See you later, then.

00:08:41.188 --> 00:08:44.984
Bye, Sakurakoji-senpai.

00:08:49.196 --> 00:08:51.866
Goodbye.

00:08:55.536 --> 00:08:57.204
She's a nice girl.

00:08:57.413 --> 00:08:58.581
Yeah.

00:08:58.789 --> 00:09:02.334
Apparently her class loves her
and puts her on a pedestal.

00:09:02.543 --> 00:09:04.712
| wonder what it's like.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:06.589
It probably puts pressure on her.

00:09:06.797 --> 00:09:12.636
Maybe. She's probably relieved to have you.

00:09:12.845 --> 00:09:14.930
| hope so.

00:09:33.908 --> 00:09:37.453
"You can do it!"

00:09:39.121 --> 00:09:42.291
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:09:53.969 --> 00:09:56.972
"New Student Information"

00:10:13.864 --> 00:10:16.867
"Sorry, I'm going to be late tonight.
We'll talk another time."

00:11:00.536 --> 00:11:03.414
I'm proud of you, Brother.

00:11:11.005 --> 00:11:14.008
It's as though they're back to spring again.

00:11:14.216 --> 00:11:15.176
Huh?

00:11:15.384 --> 00:11:16.760
Mashiki-san and Mishima-kun.

00:11:16.969 --> 00:11:18.762
Oh.

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:20.931
Things haven't changed?

00:11:21.140 --> 00:11:26.979
Nope. Did Mashiki say anything to you?

00:11:27.188 --> 00:11:33.694
| see. You think it's my fault
for getting involved like that?

00:11:33.903 --> 00:11:38.115
She's the only one who knows the truth.

00:11:38.324 --> 00:11:41.535
Class rep, that sounded kinda cool.

00:11:41.744 --> 00:11:43.037
Be serious.

00:11:43.245 --> 00:11:47.833
Okay, okay. But don't
you want it to work out?

00:11:48.042 --> 00:11:49.543
Even if it means being nosy.

00:11:49.752 --> 00:11:54.298
It's not nosy. I feel the same way.

00:11:54.506 --> 00:11:56.133
So cheer up.

00:11:56.342 --> 00:11:58.844
Let's finish this.

00:11:59.053 --> 00:12:03.349
| might cheer up if you
go on a date with me.

00:12:03.557 --> 00:12:04.475
Don't get ahead of yourself.

00:12:04.683 --> 00:12:06.435
That was close.

00:12:25.037 --> 00:12:25.871
"Student Council Room"

00:12:25.871 --> 00:12:27.039
"Student Council Room"
Did Mikado ask you to come?

00:12:27.039 --> 00:12:27.248
"Student Council Room"

00:12:27.248 --> 00:12:28.332
"Student Council Room"
Oh, no.

00:12:28.332 --> 00:12:28.457
"Student Council Room"

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.209
I'm locking up.

00:12:30.417 --> 00:12:34.380
Uh, I was just wondering if
| could help with anything.

00:12:34.588 --> 00:12:38.842
Well, the biggest thing you
could do to help Mikado

00:12:39.051 --> 00:12:41.345
would be to run in the election.

00:12:41.553 --> 00:12:44.098
Me? I can't.

00:12:44.306 --> 00:12:46.767
Kisaki's the best candidate in my class.

00:12:46.976 --> 00:12:48.560
Kisaki?

00:12:48.769 --> 00:12:51.939
She's in your class, huh?

00:12:52.147 --> 00:12:54.108
| don't know how she feels about it,

00:12:54.316 --> 00:12:57.987
but the election officials are
trying really hard to convince her.

00:12:58.195 --> 00:13:01.031
And there's Nakajima-senpai.

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:02.992
The two of them are...

00:13:03.200 --> 00:13:07.037
Well, they're... together, right?

00:13:07.246 --> 00:13:08.372
What?

00:13:08.580 --> 00:13:11.625
Oh. Oh...

00:13:11.834 --> 00:13:13.502
Is that how it seems to you?

00:13:13.711 --> 00:13:15.087
Well, yeah.

00:13:15.296 --> 00:13:17.256
Of course it does.

00:13:17.464 --> 00:13:18.882
You're right.

00:13:19.091 --> 00:13:20.718
What?

00:13:22.094 --> 00:13:24.430
Please, I'm begging you!

00:13:24.638 --> 00:13:25.931
I'm sorry.

00:13:26.140 --> 00:13:28.684
Kisaki-san, you're the perfect candidate.

00:13:28.892 --> 00:13:31.270
Aren't you and Nakajima-senpai close?

00:13:31.478 --> 00:13:36.483
I'm shy. I couldn't run in an election.

00:13:36.692 --> 00:13:39.278
Really? That's too bad.

00:13:39.486 --> 00:13:42.865
Well, I can't force you to do it.

00:13:43.073 --> 00:13:43.907
I'm sorry.

00:13:44.116 --> 00:13:46.118
No, I'm sorry, too.

00:13:46.327 --> 00:13:48.495
| just thought if you were elected,

00:13:48.704 --> 00:13:51.123
Nakajima-senpai could
leave with peace of mind.

00:13:51.332 --> 00:13:53.000
Besides, you won't get to
see each other anymore.

00:13:53.208 --> 00:13:55.044
What?

00:14:04.845 --> 00:14:06.764
Brother!

00:14:43.926 --> 00:14:46.553
| don't know who told you,

00:14:46.762 --> 00:14:48.847
but I should've told them
not to say anything.

00:14:49.056 --> 00:14:50.766
Why?

00:14:50.974 --> 00:14:52.851
Why didn't you say anything?

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.604
This is important.

00:14:55.813 --> 00:14:56.647
Sorry.

00:14:56.855 --> 00:14:59.024
I'm not asking you to apologize.

00:14:59.233 --> 00:15:01.485
Hokkaido...

00:15:01.693 --> 00:15:04.780
Are you moving out?

00:15:04.988 --> 00:15:08.325
| always intended to.

00:15:08.534 --> 00:15:11.412
You can't live in Tokyo? No matter what?

00:15:11.620 --> 00:15:13.080
We won't be able to see each other.

00:15:13.288 --> 00:15:14.957
| won't be able to visit you at your house.

00:15:15.165 --> 00:15:16.583
We won't be able to talk about our worries

00:15:16.792 --> 00:15:20.462
or buy snacks and eat them together anymore.

00:15:20.671 --> 00:15:22.923
| don't want that.

00:15:23.132 --> 00:15:26.009
Stay with me.

00:15:29.304 --> 00:15:32.182
| wish I could stay, too.

00:15:32.391 --> 00:15:33.809
I've watched you this whole time.

00:15:34.017 --> 00:15:35.853
| stood by your side and protected you.

00:15:36.061 --> 00:15:38.564
But you don't understand.

00:15:38.772 --> 00:15:39.440
Brother?

00:15:39.648 --> 00:15:40.649
No!

00:15:40.858 --> 00:15:42.860
I'm not your brother.

00:15:43.068 --> 00:15:47.030
| can't see you that way
anymore! I've always...

00:16:00.752 --> 00:16:03.088
| love you.

00:16:51.428 --> 00:16:53.222
Are you okay?

00:16:54.306 --> 00:16:57.893
Oh, yeah. I just didn't get enough sleep.

00:16:58.101 --> 00:16:59.436
Not enough sleep?

00:16:59.645 --> 00:17:01.230
Don't you have practice?

00:17:01.438 --> 00:17:04.733
Thanks. You can go now.

00:17:04.942 --> 00:17:06.235
I'm worried about you.

00:17:06.443 --> 00:17:10.614
| don't know if I'm being
helpful, but I'll do my best.

00:17:12.199 --> 00:17:16.453
I'm sure things would work out
if I were as honest as you.

00:17:16.662 --> 00:17:17.829
What?

00:17:18.038 --> 00:17:20.624
Have you heard about that bridge?

00:17:20.832 --> 00:17:22.000
Heard what?

00:17:22.209 --> 00:17:26.505
When I was a first-year, there
was a rumor going around.

00:17:26.713 --> 00:17:29.258
If a boy and a girl crossed
the bridge together at dusk,

00:17:29.466 --> 00:17:32.261
they'd be together forever.

00:17:32.469 --> 00:17:34.721
It was just a rumor,

00:17:34.930 --> 00:17:40.561
but if I were as honest as you,
God might've smiled on me.

00:17:40.769 --> 00:17:44.690
You don't believe the rumor?

00:17:44.898 --> 00:17:49.361
God abandoned me long ago.

00:18:01.873 --> 00:18:04.042
Kisaki.

00:18:04.251 --> 00:18:06.670
Mishima-kun.

00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:10.591
Thanks for the food.

00:18:10.799 --> 00:18:13.010
Actually, are you sure?

00:18:13.218 --> 00:18:15.345
There's no need for restraint. Go ahead.

00:18:15.554 --> 00:18:17.055
Thanks.

00:18:23.520 --> 00:18:27.065
Uh, sorry I got in the way.

00:18:27.274 --> 00:18:27.983
In the way?

00:18:28.191 --> 00:18:29.818
Oh, um...

00:18:30.027 --> 00:18:31.570
You're not in the way.

00:18:31.778 --> 00:18:33.697
You're helping, right?

00:18:33.905 --> 00:18:37.159
What? Uh, yeah. Sometimes.

00:18:37.367 --> 00:18:41.038
I'm sure he appreciates it.
He's busy right now.

00:18:41.246 --> 00:18:42.998
Yeah, he is.

00:18:43.206 --> 00:18:45.709
You mean with the election
and entrance exams?

00:18:45.917 --> 00:18:47.878
I'm not sure.

00:18:48.086 --> 00:18:52.799
He doesn't tell me much
about that kind of thing.

00:18:55.510 --> 00:18:58.055
He's always perfect.

00:18:58.263 --> 00:19:01.308
He seems like someone who
keeps his feelings hidden.

00:19:01.516 --> 00:19:07.147
If he ever explodes, it will have to be
something really big that sets him off.

00:19:07.356 --> 00:19:08.398
Oh, sorry.

00:19:08.607 --> 00:19:12.402
I'm sure you know more about that than I do.

00:19:47.646 --> 00:19:49.106
Hey.

00:19:49.314 --> 00:19:50.315
Good morning.

00:19:50.524 --> 00:19:52.901
You're moving slowly today, President.

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:56.613
| do sometimes.
| can't allow myself to fall apart.

00:19:56.822 --> 00:19:58.615
| couldn't agree more.

00:20:04.538 --> 00:20:07.165
Vote for me!

00:20:07.374 --> 00:20:08.375
Thank you!

00:20:08.583 --> 00:20:10.836
They're campaigning.

00:20:11.044 --> 00:20:12.504
Mikado.

00:20:20.637 --> 00:20:23.724
This is a sudden development.

00:20:27.018 --> 00:20:29.646
"Vice President Candidate Kisaki Waka"

00:20:30.897 --> 00:20:33.984
"Vice President Candidate Kisaki Waka"

00:20:34.067 --> 00:20:40.657
The class 1-1 election
speeches will now begin.

00:20:40.866 --> 00:20:45.787
I'm student council vice president
candidate Kisaki Waka.

00:20:45.996 --> 00:20:47.914
She's doing this for you.

00:20:48.123 --> 00:20:49.249
What?

00:20:50.041 --> 00:20:53.378
| intend to carry on the
current president's will

00:20:53.587 --> 00:20:56.465
and support the new student council president

00:20:56.673 --> 00:20:57.132
--as I lead future students to ever greater heights...

00:20:57.132 --> 00:20:59.426
--Senpai, I was surprised.
--as I lead future students to ever greater heights...

00:20:59.634 --> 00:21:02.262
We were suddenly notified
in a class e-mail last night.

00:21:02.471 --> 00:21:04.598
| hope you'll vote for her.

00:21:04.890 --> 00:21:06.767
"I will carry on President Nakajima's will and create
the student council of the future. Class 1-1 Kisaki Waka"

00:21:06.767 --> 00:21:08.894
“I will continue the promises and systems improved upon by President Nakajima. | will
establish a suggestion box and implement and enact as many of your suggestions as possible."”

00:21:15.901 --> 00:21:19.237
Hey, Mishima! Quit slacking off!

00:21:19.446 --> 00:21:21.698
Excuse me.

00:21:37.088 --> 00:21:39.174
Vote for Kisaki.

00:21:52.395 --> 00:21:53.814
Hey.

00:21:56.274 --> 00:21:58.151
Good morning.

00:21:59.778 --> 00:22:01.488
Good morning.

00:22:10.539 --> 00:22:19.047
Another city light blinks out

00:22:19.256 --> 00:22:28.890
Seems I'm the only one
being left behind like this

00:22:29.099 --> 00:22:37.607
I leaned in close to the light
of the vending machine

00:22:37.816 --> 00:22:46.741
And bought something
other than my usual coffee

00:22:46.950 --> 00:22:51.413
I wonder if I can be myself

00:22:51.621 --> 00:22:57.460
From now on, and even further beyond

00:22:58.587 --> 00:23:07.554
Surely someday we'll come
to know sadness as love

00:23:07.762 --> 00:23:16.897
Reconnecting somewhere
and parting again, over and over

00:23:17.105 --> 00:23:30.660
Surely the day will come when we're
all too used to feeling joy

00:23:30.869 --> 00:23:37.208
Call that happiness

00:23:40.045 --> 00:23:41.421
"Next Time"

00:23:41.421 --> 00:23:47.135
